dev/render.html paintLayer(): give GRADIENT_ANGULAR its own branch that draws on a canvas using the paint's full transform, instead of letting it fall through to radialGradient. (GRADIENT_DIAMOND can keep the radial approximation, or get a marker.)

```js
if (p.type === 'GRADIENT_ANGULAR') {
  const wrap = document.createElement('div'); wrap.className = 'layer'; wrap.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  const cv = document.createElement('canvas'); cv.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%';
  wrap.appendChild(cv);
  requestAnimationFrame(() => {               // size is known after layout (or pass w,h from build())
    const w = wrap.clientWidth, h = wrap.clientHeight, dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;
    cv.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(w * dpr)); cv.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(h * dpr));
    const ctx = cv.getContext('2d');
    const inv = invert(p.gradientTransform);  // gradient space -> normalised layer space
    // gradient space -> canvas pixels: diag(w,h)*dpr * inv
    ctx.setTransform(w*dpr*inv[0][0], h*dpr*inv[1][0], w*dpr*inv[0][1], h*dpr*inv[1][1], w*dpr*inv[0][2], h*dpr*inv[1][2]);
    // Figma angular: centre (0.5,0.5) in gradient space, starts along +x (3 o'clock), clockwise in y-down
    // == canvas createConicGradient(0, cx, cy) semantics
    const g = ctx.createConicGradient(0, 0.5, 0.5);
    for (const s of p.gradientStops) g.addColorStop(Math.min(1, Math.max(0, s.position)), rgba(s.color));
    ctx.fillStyle = g;
    ctx.fillRect(-1e3, -1e3, 2e3, 2e3);       // covers the layer in gradient units for any sane transform
  });
  return wrap;
}
```

This keeps Figma's stretch-to-box behaviour, because the transform goes through the normalised w×h space, and it honours any rotation or centre offset the plugin encodes.

